course: dictionary
lesson: 15837
title: Undesirable: not wanted
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Undesirable means not wanted, because it is bad, harmful or unpleasant. Break it into parts: un- means not, and desirable means worth wanting. So undesirable means not worth wanting.
explain: «The medicine had undesirable side effects, such as feeling sick.» The side effects are bad things the medicine causes, so nobody wants them. Ask yourself: what is the opposite? Desirable means something good that you would want.
explain: In formal writing, «It is undesirable to stay up late» means «It is not a good idea to stay up late.» When you meet it in a test, swap in «not a good idea» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Undesirable is an adjective: it describes a noun, as in an undesirable side effect.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so undesirable means not desirable.
fact: «Undesirable» means bad, harmful or unpleasant, so people do not want it.
fact: «Highly undesirable» means very bad, or very much not wanted.
fact: As an old-fashioned noun, «an undesirable» can mean a person thought to be unwanted in a place. This use is rare today and is unkind.
exercise: «The medicine had undesirable side effects.» What does undesirable mean here? | *Bad and unpleasant, so nobody wants them | Very tasty | Easy to find in a shop | Good for your teeth
exercise: In «It is undesirable to eat sweets before dinner», what does undesirable mean? | *Not a good idea | Very cheap | Finished at last | Hard to chew
exercise: Which word is the opposite of undesirable? | *Desirable | Unpleasant | Unwanted | Harmful
test: Weeds are undesirable in a vegetable garden. What does this tell you? | They are the same as the vegetables | They only grow in the sea | Gardeners love them and plant more | *Nobody wants them there, because they harm the plants
test: Which word uses the prefix un- to mean not, like undesirable? | *Unkind, meaning not kind | Brave | Gentle | Pleasant
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The factory released undesirable smoke into the air»? | Loud and fast | *Harmful and not wanted | Warm and soft | Clean and clear
